    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0308" n="232" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1891</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Russell to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-07T09:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 7, 1916, 9 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The 4th Regiment of Marines which left Monte Cristi on June 26 reached Santiago
                    last night and entered the town without opposition. Encountering considerable
                    resistance from troops which were strongly entrenched in several places. Our
                    forces from Puerto Plata left along the line of railway to make junction with
                    the 4th Regiment and had several encounters, total casualties on the whole
                    expedition including operation from Puerto Plata, three privates killed,
                    thirteen privates wounded and two officers wounded. Arias has surrendered to
                    Governor of Santiago; his forces were deserting him and the people of North were
                    tired of him. Arias has telegraphed Archbishop requesting permission to come to
                    the capital. This, of course, will not be allowed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
